ek 12?","published":"2026-11-23T12:14:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50545207/2026-college-football-power-rankings-top-25-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Tennessee fined by SEC after fans throw golf balls on field","description":"Tennessee was fined $250,000 by the SEC after fans threw golf balls and mustard bottles onto the football field late during Saturday's win over LSU.","published":"2026-11-23T01:42:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50568028/tennessee-fined-sec-fans-throw-golf-balls-field","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Notre Dame loses safety Luke Talich to torn Achilles","description":"Notre Dame starting safety Luke Talich sustained a torn right Achilles tendon in Saturday's win against SMU, sources told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-22T23:15:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50566676/notre-dame-loses-safety-luke-talich-torn-achilles","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What Week 12's unexpected results mean for Rivalry Week and beyond","description":"After another chaotic weekend, we look at the playoff and conference races on the line with one game to go.","published":"2026-11-22T23:54:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50563018/week-12-results-rivalry-week","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 recruit AJ Randle Jr. flips from Miami to Notre Dame","description":"Notre Dame coach Marcus Freeman flipped Miami pledge AJ Randle Jr., ESPN's No. 9 outside linebacker in the 2027 recruiting class, to fill a late-cycle need.","published":"2026-11-22T22:48:18.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50565158/2027-recruit-aj-randle-jr-flips-miami-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Pac-12 reveals unique flex schedule for season's final week","description":"The Pac-12 announced its unique flex schedule for the final week of the regular season early Sunday morning.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564960/pac-12-reveals-unique-flex-schedule-season-final-week","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Montana State ranked No. 1, 5-7 LIU makes FCS bracket as conference champ","description":"Defending national champion Montana State received the top seed for the 24-team FCS playoffs, while Northeast Conference champion LIU (5-7) became the first playoff team with a losing record since 2017.","published":"2026-11-23T00:02:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564910/montana-state-grabs-top-seed-24-team-fcs-playoff-bracket","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5141684/austin-simmons","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austin_Simmons"},"pick":{"pick":50,"round":2,"team":"SEA","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Austin Simmons","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austin_Simmons","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:17:43Z","intro":"Austin David Simmons (born November 8, 2005) is an American college football quarterback for the Missouri Tigers. He previously played for the Ole Miss Rebels. He also played for the Ole Miss Rebels baseball team.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Simmons attended Pahokee High School in Pahokee, Florida before transferring to Moore Haven Junior Senior High School in Moore Haven, Florida. As a sophomore he passed for 3,253 yards and 27 touchdowns. Simmons reclassified from the 2025 to 2023 recruiting class. He originally committed to play college football at the University of Florida before changing his commitment to the University of Mississippi.\nWhile enrolled in high school, Simmons was also enrolled and earning college credits at Miami Dade College, completing an associate degree from that school before turning 17. He received a bachelor's degree from Ole Miss in May 2025."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"2023 SEASON\nSimmons was the third-string quarterback throughout 2023 season. As a result, Simmons was redshirted. After the season, he appeared in 13 games as a relief pitcher on the baseball team, going 2–0 with 3.21 earned run average (ERA) with 20 strikeouts over 14 innings pitched.\n\n2024 SEASON\nSimmons began his redshirt freshman year in 2024 as the backup to senior quarterback Jaxson Dart. In his first collegiate game, he recorded 7 completions, 111 yards, and he threw his first career touchdown pass. He made minor appearances in relief against Middle Tennessee State, Wake Forest, Georgia Southern, and Kentucky before helping the Rebels break or tie single-game team passing records in yards and touchdowns against Arkansas, Simmons threw for 47 yards and a touchdown finishing an Ole Miss victory of 63-32. On November 9, 2024, Simmons came off the bench versus Georgia for a crucial first quarter drive following a minor injury to Jaxson Dart, Simmons went 5-of-6 for 64 yards and led his team to the endzone ultimately giving the Rebels the offensive spark they needed to get a 28-10 victory.\n\n2025 SEASON\nSimmons began his third year as the Rebels' starting quarterback. He passed for 341 yards and 3 touchdowns in their week 1 victory over Georgia State. In week 2 against Kentucky, Simmons left the game with an ankle injury, forcing backup Trinidad Chambliss to finish the 30-23 win over the Wildcats. Due to Simmons's injury, Chambliss started against Arkansas the following week, and took over the starting quarterback role for the rest of the season.\nSimmons saw limited action for the remainder of 2025. From week 3 onward, he appeared in 4 games, completing 12 of 20 passes for 168 yards and a single touchdown in that span.\nOn January 2, 2026, Simmons announced his intention to enter the transfer portal. On January 6, 2026, he signed with the Missouri Tigers. Despite signing at Missouri, Simmons opted to remain with the Ole Miss Rebels for the remainder of their College Football Playoff run.\n\n2026 SEASON\nIn Week 5 against No. 8 Florida, Simmons went 23 of 30 for 340 yards and two touchdowns in a 45–17 victory."}]}}